.mjs;tools/gates/prefreeze.sh;tools/gates/sandbox-run.sh;tools/gates/tests/sandbox.test.mjs;tools/agents/tests/test_run_meta.py;tools/agents/tests/test_agent_settings.py;docs/delivery/environment.md,"AN-10 (F-DG0-009): the pre-freeze check tools/gates/prefreeze.sh (round-5 repair) is the orchestrator's integration check before a candidate freezes. AN-11 (F-DG0-232): D-026 now names it; since the round-12 repair it runs the candidate checks sandboxed against the committed HEAD. The AN-10 known defect (directory arguments to node --test) was fixed in the orchestrator's prefreeze glob fix, which now passes file globs; AN-11 also repairs this row's part-file notes cell, which had been left unquoted and broke the merge. Open: the CI bubblewrap step has not yet run on a hosted runner, so the CI part of this acceptance is unverified until the first workflow run on the branch reports (D-026, environment.md). AN-12 correction: nested bubblewrap is available inside the agent sandbox (the orchestrator ran bwrap and tools/gates/tests/sandbox.test.mjs from a sandboxed session); the earlier note that it was unavailable was wrong. prefreeze.sh checks the committed HEAD, so it is run after committing. The register-equals-merge pre-freeze check (D-026) closes the part-file/register divergence AN-11 reported. AN-13 (D-027, F-DG0-141): sandbox-run.sh no longer clones into the agent-writable $TMPDIR (/tmp/claude-0) or runs git checkout outside bubblewrap; procedure and acceptance now describe the in-sandbox clone on a private tmpfs with the git directory bound read-only, and cite the F-DG0-141 regression test. Sandboxed dependency installation from P1 is a separate requirement, REQ-DLV-042. AN-14 (D-028): since each agent run now has its own private TMPDIR, agents no longer share $TMPDIR; the procedure's wording was updated accordingly (the private tmpfs of sandbox-run.sh is unchanged)."
REQ-DLV-042,ENGINEERING,"Install dependencies only inside an OS sandbox: the orchestrator's install step runs under bubblewrap with network limited to the package registry, a read-only root filesystem, only the target tree and package store writable, lifecycle scripts disabled unless allow-listed, and a committed lockfile",M0012;M0314;M0331;M0404,§0.1 Verify capabilities and establish the workspace; §16 Technology and dependency pinning; §16 Security; §21 P1 Architecture and working foundation,,Lockfile (committed);Package manifest;Package registry host;Lifecycle-script allow-list;Target tree;Package store path,"Agent shells have no network (D-025), so dependency installation is an orchestrator step. The orchestrator never runs it with its own unconfined privileges: an installation wrapper (delivered and tested in P1 before the first install) runs the package manager inside bubblewrap with network allowed for the package registry, the root filesystem read-only, only the target tree (for example node_modules or the virtual environment) and the package store writable, package lifecycle scripts (install/postinstall and similar) disabled unless the package is on a reviewed allow-list, and a frozen install from the committed lockfile (the install fails if the lockfile is missing or would change); later build and test commands that execute installed package code also run only inside the sandbox (D-026, D-027, F-DG0-142)","Sandboxed installation wrapper, lifecycle-script allow-list, committed lockfile and wrapper tests",devops-engineer;delivery-orchestrator,"write:delivery-orchestrator(delivery records),assigned implementer(scoped paths); review:domain-reviewer,code-security-reviewer,qa-verifier; gate-decision:release-auditor; view:all project agents",Installation wrapper invoked by the orchestrator (and by CI) for every dependency install,"installation wrapper script and its tests (planned P1 names, fixed by the P1 ADRs); lockfile; lifecycle-script allow-list","A18;A23;A24: the P1 wrapper tests show, under the wrapper, that (1) a write outside the target tree and package store fails with a read-only filesystem error; (2) a package lifecycle script not on the allow-list does not run, while an allow-listed one does; (3) an install without a committed lockfile, or one that would change the lockfile, fails non-zero; (4) a missing bubblewrap makes the wrapper exit non-zero (BLOCKED, never an unsandboxed install); and the first dependency install of P1 is shown in the run evidence to have gone through the wrapper",P1,DG1,IMPLEMENTED,tools/deps/install-sandbox.sh;tools/deps/tests/install-sandbox.test.sh;docs/delivery/test-evidence/DG1/orchestrator/install-sandbox-acceptance.log;docs/delivery/decisions.md,"implementation-assumption: the mechanism (bubblewrap, registry-only network, read-only root, writable target tree and package store, lifecycle scripts off unless allow-listed) is the orchestrator's implementation decision D-027 in response to F-DG0-142 (docs/delivery/threat-model.md residual 3), not master-prompt text. The source grounding is M0012 (do not weaken existing permission controls to enable the workflow: the agent sandbox of D-025 must not be bypassed by an unconfined install), M0314 (pin compatible versions and lockfiles), M0331 (dependency checks) and M0404 (P1 repo/build/CI). Classified P1/DG1 per the §21 stage table: the first dependency install happens in P1 (repo/build/CI, M0404), and DG0 installs none. Residual (threat model 3): the content of the installed packages themselves; package code executes only inside the sandbox. Related: REQ-S16-009 (pinning and licence inventory, DG7), REQ-S19-003 (handover manifests and lockfiles). DG1 analyst check (T-DG1-REG): acceptance suite 7/7. The first-real-install element rests on the D-046 record (no separate install log). Registry-only egress depends on the environment network policy (D-046 residual)."
